[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="CompanionResource" load_steps=2 format=3 uid="uid://cmbrvlcompwren"]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/Companions/CompanionResource.cs" id="1_companion"]

; Wren Halloway, the caravan yard's hired sword (Phase 38R) — the second companion in the game and
; the first who joins for money rather than for a reason.
;
; ⚠️ NO LoyaltyQuestId is the design. Kael is deepened by his brother's quest; a mercenary is
; recruited by a purse and has no story to be owed. Authoring an empty loyalty quest id says so —
; --validate checks it only if it is set, so a hopeful placeholder would be a broken reference rather
; than a promise.
;
; StartingLoyalty 25 against Kael's 40, and that is the whole characterisation in one number: she is
; bought, not sworn, so she starts colder than the man who volunteered. Nothing in 38R spends it —
; CompanionLoyaltyComponent already moves it in play — but a hire that started as loyal as an oath
; would quietly say the coin meant nothing.
;
; The body is npc_adventurer_f, already adopted and already retargeted (GeneralSkeleton, so the shared
; animation library binds). ⚠️ It is the same model Sera wears in the Embermarket — allowed here
; because 38Q2's rule is about two identical models IN ONE FRAME, and these two stand in different
; cells two hundred metres apart. Rendered at eye level, front and back, beside the two guild-body
; wardens she shares the yard with before it was adopted.

[resource]
